      {
        "id": 163813,
        "name": "JimmyTheCannon",
        "username": "JimmyTheCannon",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/j/cdc98d/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2016-03-07T03:28:27.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Okay, that didn't go so well. I got a Fine on my third try - the first one was an unmitigated disaster and the second wasn't much better.</p><p>First round was to set up Chrono-Ranger and AZ to take out the Dark Hero, done with a \"By Any Means\" on him, and getting the Psychic Reduction plating out for Omni-X (or any 4-damage plating). With that done, make sure the Whipacorn doesn't hit Omni on the second turn - he's going to Defensive Blast to wipe out all enemy targets *without* hitting the Dreamer. If you take out Illusory Demon last after all other targets *except* Dreamer, its death effect will destroy Defensive Blast so Dreamer doesn't take damage. You have to throw By Any Means on the Grotesque Arachnoid first so that it'll take 8 damage instead of 4, and make sure everything else is at or as close to 4 as possible - I had a Toy Master still up but AZ finished him right after.</p><p>Getting her to flip that early with everyone still at 20+ HP made the game a lot easier. Temporal Grenade removed Char easily; after that it was just killing her projections as quickly as possible to stack them up underneath her. Sucker Punch removed the Treacherous Ape before he could do damage to anyone other than Tachyon (I think I actually got it from playing Nimble Strike while she couldn't deal damage just to get the card draw). The rest was a couple of Sonic Vortexes, lots of little shots and bounties from Chrono-Ranger, and another Defensive Blast (this one actually hit Dreamer) although I think that one wasn't 100% necessary, I just wanted to kill as many of the projections as possible. AZ finished two off with a Frostbound Drain and his power to put her at 9 and that was the game.</p><p>Very tough fight but finished it without losing anyone that time.</p>",
