        "id": 163816,
        "name": "LewdDolphin21",
        "username": "LewdDolphin21",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/lewddolphin21/{size}/1893_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-03-07T16:00:30.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"stevelabny\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/stevelabny/48/2536_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> stevelabny:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I think I'm letting the Toy Masters and her flip scare me from playing Omni and AZ's cards.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>The Toy Master act at the start of her turn, so you have a round to deal with him before he does damage. He hits only one target, though, so it's not too bad if he does go off anyway. Her flip destroys H ongoing cards, so putting out more than H of those helps with keeping the ongoings alive that you would want to keep alive.</p>",
